    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d782-a1">

                <pb facs="0901" n="821" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg821"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton to Mr.
                            Mariscal.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-03"><hi rendition="#italic">September 3,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s esteemed note of the 16th ultimo, informing me
                    that the question of an additional article to the treaty between the two
                    countries to define the exclusive power of consular agents to take cognizance of
                    and to determine difficulties which may arise at sea or in ports between
                    captains, officers, and crews of vessels, has been referred to the consulting
                    attorney of the sections of your excellency’s department.</p>
                <p>Awaiting the information referred to in said note, I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Powell Clayton.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
